schema: '0.4'
id: metapost-01-canonical-drawing
type: image
quality: high
solution: metapost
category: 2d-canvas-svg-and-creative-coding
variant: canonical-drawing
references:
- references/fim/overview/canvas-svg-creative-animation/metapost.md
- references/fim/solution/metapost.md
prompt:
  system: Generate production-quality FIM media assets for the named 2D canvas, SVG, or creative-coding solution. Output only
    the requested source artifact with no markdown fences or explanatory prose.
  text: "Create the canonical drawing and illustration prompt for MetaPost.\n\nScenario:\nCreate an illustrated studio workbench\
    \ scene for a fictional creative systems lab. Include at least six distinct objects, two labeled callouts, a background\
    \ grid or framing device, foreground/midground/background layering, and a small legend showing the native drawing primitives\
    \ used.\n\nImplementation requirements:\n- Category: 2d-canvas-svg-and-creative-coding.\n- Required solution: metapost\
    \ (MetaPost).\n- Output: a complete MetaPost .mp source file only.\n- Native API contract: Use MetaPost beginfig/endfig\
    \ blocks, paths, pairs, equations, loops, colors, pens, labels, draw, fill, filldraw, transforms, and outputformat :=\
    \ \"svg\".\n- Native technique focus: declarative MetaPost geometry with solved point relationships, reusable macros,\
    \ precise paths, TeX-ready labels, and vector output settings.\n- Responsive contract: Define a clear figure bounding\
    \ box and scalable units; include comments describing SVG/PDF export dimensions and safe downscaling for narrow layouts.\n\
    - Export and integration contract: Set prologues := 3, outputformat := \"svg\", and outputtemplate; include compile comments\
    \ for mpost and PDF/SVG export without depending on browser code.\n- Determinism contract: Do not use uncontrolled randomness;\
    \ if variation is simulated, derive it from deterministic loop indices and documented constants.\n- Scenario-specific\
    \ emphasis: Build a polished canonical drawing or illustration that proves the solution can create a nonblank first render\
    \ with native primitives, layers, labels, and clean composition.\n- Additional edge detail: Keep the artwork mostly static,\
    \ but include one optional hover, focus, or subtle animation state if the solution supports interaction without weakening\
    \ export quality.\n- Include realistic inline sample data, labels, dimensions, seed value, and source note where the scenario\
    \ needs them.\n- Avoid placeholder lorem ipsum text, external credentials, paid private assets, and hidden dependencies.\n\
    - Output only the final artifact, with no commentary outside the artifact."
  requirements:
  - Start from a visible nonblank render state; do not require user input before the first meaningful frame.
  - Use explicit viewBox, canvas sizing, or equivalent figure bounds; handle device pixel ratio or vector scaling where relevant.
  - Use deliberate layering order so background, main subject, annotations, and controls do not collide.
  - Use accessible contrast for text, callouts, controls, and essential marks against their backgrounds.
  - Include responsive behavior and at least one export path appropriate to the solution.
  - Use deterministic randomness from a documented seed and make repeated reloads reproducible.
  - Include a concise diagnostics or source note with renderer, seed, dimensions, and export status.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
output:
  text_format: metapost
  artifact_kind: metapost-vector-source-canonical-drawing
  formats:
  - format: mp
  - format: svg
  - format: pdf
  dimensions:
    width: 1440
    height: 900
  render_expectation: A nonblank artifact suitable for browser or compiler rendering and capture after initial load or compile.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present.
  - Generated artifact uses the requested solution and does not substitute a different renderer or library for the core drawing
    work.
  - Initial render is nonblank and shows the main subject within the first viewport or figure bounds.
  - viewBox/canvas sizing or equivalent figure bounds are explicit, responsive, and not blurry at common DPR values.
  - Layering order is intentional and keeps background, dense marks, labels, controls, and export UI readable.
  - Contrast is sufficient for text, controls, callouts, and critical marks in both default and compact layouts.
  - Responsive/export behavior works for compact, wide, and capture-oriented sizes without clipping key content.
  - Deterministic randomness is seeded, documented, and reproducible across reloads for the same seed.
  - 'Solution-specific API contract is satisfied for MetaPost: declarative MetaPost geometry with solved point relationships,
    reusable macros, precise paths, TeX-ready labels, and vector output settings.'
  - 'Export/integration hooks are present where applicable: Set prologues := 3, outputformat := "svg", and outputtemplate;
    include compile comments for mpost and PDF/SVG export without depending on browser code..'
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria: YAML uses schema 0.4 with required fields, the generated artifact matches the requested text format, contains
      no markdown fences, and uses the named solution syntax or API without parse/runtime errors.
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria: The artifact satisfies the scenario, includes solution-specific native capabilities, covers nonblank rendering,
      sizing, layering, contrast, responsive/export behavior, and deterministic randomness.
  - name: Visual quality
    weight: 25
    criteria: Composition, typography, spacing, color, density, hierarchy, motion, and labels are polished, coherent, legible,
      and suited to the requested drawing, generative, brand, or integration use case.
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria: The artifact handles resize, missing or empty input, fallback states, lifecycle cleanup, export edge cases,
      performance limits, and deterministic regeneration without blank screens or broken output.
  pass_conditions:
  - Rubric weights sum to 100 with Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual quality 25, and Robustness 15.
  - Score is 80 or higher out of 100 and no rubric dimension scores zero.
  - Generated result has a nonblank render, explicit viewBox/canvas sizing or equivalent bounds, readable layering, sufficient
    contrast, responsive/export behavior, and deterministic randomness.
  - Generated content is aligned with the referenced overview and solution documents for the named solution.
tags:
- fim
- 2d-canvas-svg-and-creative-coding
- metapost
- canonical-drawing
- image
- nonblank-render
- viewbox-canvas-sizing
- deterministic-randomness
